  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Online Bureau\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Updated On Nov 13, 2026 at 03:12 PM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: India recorded a 38 per cent reduction in TB mortality since 2015, declining from 28 per lakh population in 2015 to 18 per lakh in 2025, according to the Union Health Ministry.The Centre's remarks come after the World Health Organization's (WHO) Global Tuberculosis Report 2026 found India reached the milestone of  35% mortality reduction in 2025.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>In a release, the Union Health Ministry said India achieved 94 per cent treatment success rate among patients with drug-susceptible TB attributing the progress to intensified interventions under the <a href=\"/tag/national+tb+elimination+programme\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">National TB Elimination Programme</a> (NTEP), including proactive case finding, use of AI enabled X-rays, rapid diagnostics, prompt treatment initiation, differentiated TB care, and nutritional support through the Ni-kshay Poshan Yojana and Ni-kshay Mitra initiative.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M -->\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>According to the Ministry, under the TB Mukt Bharat Abhiyaan, more than 25 crore people have been brought under intensified screening activities between December 7, 2024 and November 8, 2026. The campaign has facilitated over 11 crore chest X-rays and more than three crore nucleic acid amplification tests (NAAT).During this time, 48.64 lakh new TB cases were identified, including 14.97 lakh asymptomatic cases.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The ministry also highlighted the use of advanced technologies to make TB screening and diagnosis faster, more accurate and accessible.“The deployment of portable AI-enabled digital X-rays, expansion of rapid molecular diagnostic technologies, including NAAT, and strengthening of diagnostic infrastructure have significantly enhanced the programme's ability to reach populations across diverse geographical and social settings,” it said.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>In a social media post, WHO South-East Asia Regional Office (SEARO) recognised India's progress saying, \"India is making a significant contribution to the progress in reducing tuberculosis mortality in the WHO South-East Asia Region.\"In a release, Union Health Minister, JP Nadda described the results as encouraging and reaffirmed the Government's commitment to towards a TB-Mukt Bharat.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Nov 13, 2026 at 03:12 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Nov 13, 2026 at 08:01 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">2 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                                            <!-- <div class=\"app-store-container desktop-view\">\n                            <a href=\"/app\" title=\"\" aria-label=\"Play Store\">\n                                <img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Rel